{"fingerprint":"65501a6329ab03a163483858e79ce2ca46c5cbe8e478189f289ff2059911c3c2","path":"src/review_gauntlet/cli.py","rule_id":"data-validation","content":"validate-verdict accepts structurally invalid precise locations such as start_line=0/end_line=5 or end_line < start_line. The command tells external adapters to use it as the pre-finish validator, but CommandReviewAdapter later rejects the same ranges in _validated_comments_for_cell, so an adapter can see validation pass and still fail the review run. Mirror the adapter's basic line-range validation here for non-imprecise comments.","suggestion_code":"        payload = validate_verdict_json(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
